<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH JUNE OUTPUT SEEN UP 3.2 PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>DUTCH JUNE OUTPUT SEEN UP 3.2 PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists expect the</p>
<p>year-on-year manufacturing production figure for June, due on</p>
<p>Thursday, to rise 3.2 percent.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT--Date-Period-Indicator------------Consensus--Range------Pvs</p>
<p> 0730 14/8 June   Manufac. output M/M   1.7 pct    0.0/3.0   0.4</p>
<p> 0730 14/8 June   Manufac. output Y/Y   3.2 pct    1.7/5.0   4.1</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING,</p>
<p>MeesPierson, NIB Securities, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
